WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.934
-Joining me now is the star

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.102
of "Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:06.106
which airs Thursday nights
on NBC.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:09.775
Here's the one, the only,
Andy Samberg!

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:11.077
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.911
-Andy!
Oh, my goodness!

00:00:12.911 --> 00:00:16.215
Ah! Look at you, wow!

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:18.752
Looking good, bud.
How are ya?

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.186
-I'm good. How are you?
-I'm great.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.754
I miss you, man.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.456
I'm so happy that you're here
on the show.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.991
I wanted to play
a fun game with you

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.493
because I know
you're a great songwriter

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.128
and I'm assuming
that you probably know a lot

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:32.231
about famous songs,
so I want to put

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:34.033
[ Laughter ]
your music knowledge to the test

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.836
in a game called
"Misname That Song."

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.471
Here we go.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.274
♪ Misname that song ♪

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.641
♪ Misname that ♪

00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:44.977
♪ Song ♪

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:47.480
-[ Laughing ]
Now, Andy,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.748
in front of each of us are

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:52.185
the incorrect names
of a number of famous songs.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:55.421
All of these names are close
to the actual name of the song,

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.223
but not quite right.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.658
When it's your turn,
you'll read out

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.726
the messed up version
of that song title,

00:01:00.726 --> 00:01:03.362
then, the other person tries
to guess the correct song title,

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.264
based on only that clue.

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:06.966
We have to guess
as many songs as possible

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.468
before the timer runs out.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.102
Are you ready for this?

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.671
-I couldn't be more ready.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.839
-Yeah.
-I was born for this.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.106
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, I know you were, yeah.

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:15.775
Well Andy,
since you are my guest,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.210
you're going to guess
first, okay?

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:21.247 line:0%
Let's put 45 seconds
on the clock.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.615 line:0%
We got this, buddy.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.117 line:0%
And here we go.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.791 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-"Driver's License."

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.825 line:0%
-That's correct.
[ Ding ]

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.961 line:0%
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:43.469 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:44.938 line:0%
-"Goodbye Thrice?"

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.739 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:50.543 line:0%
-"Goodbye Thrice"
is not the song, nope.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.411 line:0%
-"Bye, Bye, Bye."
-Yes, that's correct.
[ Ding ]

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:54.314 line:0%
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.919 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:05.124 line:0%
-"I exist on a vessel
that floats in water"?

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.193 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.428 line:0%
-You should really --
-"I'm on a Boat"?

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.629 line:0%
-Yes, "I'm on a Boat"!
[ Ding ]

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:10.830 line:0%
[ Cheering and applause ]
That's by you!

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.398 line:0%
You wrote that!
Okay.

00:02:13.398 --> 00:02:14.767 line:0%
[ Buzzer ]
Ugh!

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.035 line:0%
Alright.
Not bad.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.603 line:0%
-Excuse me.
-Three.

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:19.071 line:0%
Three is the magic number.

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:21.074
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:22.708
Sorry.
A little rusty in there.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.510
I was a little rusty,
there, Andy.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.679
It is now my turn.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:29.348 line:0%
Let's put another 45 seconds
on the clock.

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:30.583 line:0%
-Okay.
-Whenever you're ready,

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.952 line:0%
go ahead and read
the misnamed song title.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.220 line:0%
Here we go.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.389 line:0%
-You ready?
-Yeah, I'm so ready.

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:39.392 line:0%
[ Suspenseful music plays ]
-Okay.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.928 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.395 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:44.697 line:0%
-"Dancing Queen."
[ Ding ]

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.700 line:0%
[ Cheering
and applause ]

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.070 line:0%
